Coded Kevin Payne on `school-vouchers` as rung 5 (universal vouchers), based on his co-sponsorship and Y vote on HB2853 (2022), which added ARS §15-2401.01 making ESA eligibility universal — matching the annex's rung-5 example type exactly. Since the vote/sponsorship occurred during his House term (2017–2023) in the same legislature he now serves in as Senator, it counts as `in-term` under the V5 earlier-chamber ruling. Written to `labels/coder-3.json`.
